// `std.rand`: the home of randomness' host interface, `std.rand.Eff`, whose
// operation draws fair bits from the entropy source of the operating system.
// A source names the interface where it imports this module,
// `import std.rand;`, and nowhere else. The interface is native, so no
// declaration here states it. `lcg` is a second model of the interface: a
// seeded generator, written in the language, answers the same draws.
//
// One program then runs under three models. `gandr run` answers its draws
// from the host's entropy. `lcg` answers them from a fixed seed, so each run
// gives the same draws. The corpus's exact model answers each sequence of
// draws once and weighs each path.
//
// `lcg` steps a linear congruential generator, `x' = (a · x + c) mod 2^w`.
// It answers a draw of `n` bits with the top `n` bits of the new state, the
// state divided by `2^(w - n)`. Its constants are those of Knuth's MMIX: `c`
// is odd and `a mod 4 = 1`. So the state runs through all `2^w` values
// before it repeats.
//
// The handler keeps the last width and its divisor beside the state. A draw
// at the same width again costs one multiplication, one addition, one
// `int.mod` and one `int.div`. `lcg` passes each draw that it cannot answer
// to the model outside it, unchanged. A generator width outside 1 to 64 also
// sends a draw of that width outside. So the host refuses each such width by
// name.
//
// Limits: a draw wider than the generator gets its answer from the model
// outside it. The capability of randomness and distributions wait for demand.
//
// - see: #5707
// - see: #5713
// - see: Knuth, The Art of Computer Programming, volume 2, § 3.2.1 — the
//   conditions for a full period

/// `2^w` for a width `w` from 0 to 71: `2^(8q) · 2^r` for `w = 8q + r`. A draw
/// of `w` bits takes `2^w` values.
pub def span(w : Integer) -> Integer =
  let low : Integer = match int.mod w 8 where
    | 0 => 1
    | 1 => 2
    | 2 => 4
    | 3 => 8
    | 4 => 16
    | 5 => 32
    | 6 => 64
    | _ => 128
  let high : Integer = match int.div w 8 where
    | 0 => 1
    | 1 => 256
    | 2 => 65536
    | 3 => 16777216
    | 4 => 4294967296
    | 5 => 1099511627776
    | 6 => 281474976710656
    | 7 => 72057594037927936
    | _ => 18446744073709551616
  high * low

/// `lcg` answers each draw of `n` bits in `body` with the top `n` bits of the
/// next state, from the state `seed`. Each draw outside `1 ≤ n ≤ w ≤ 64`
/// passes to the model outside `lcg`.
pub def lcg[a : Type](w : Integer, seed : Integer, body : () -> [std.rand.Eff] a) -> [std.rand.Eff] a =
  match 1 <= w && w <= 64 where
    | false => {
      let _ = std.rand.draw w;
      force body
    }
    | true => {
      let modulus = span w;
      let stepped : Integer -> (Integer -> (Integer -> [std.rand.Eff] a)) = handle r : std.rand.Eff {
        let x = force body;
        pure fun (state : Integer) {
          pure fun (last : Integer) { pure fun (divisor : Integer) { pure x } }
        }
      } with {
        | pure(x) => pure x
        | oper draw(n, k) => pure fun (state : Integer) {
          pure fun (last : Integer) { pure fun (divisor : Integer) {
            match n == last where
              | true => {
                let next = int.mod (6364136223846793005 * state + 1442695040888963407) modulus;
                let g = k (int.div next divisor);
                let g1 = g next;
                let g2 = g1 last;
                g2 divisor
              }
              | false => match 1 <= n && n <= w where
                | true => {
                  let d = span (w - n);
                  let next = int.mod (6364136223846793005 * state + 1442695040888963407) modulus;
                  let g = k (int.div next d);
                  let g1 = g next;
                  let g2 = g1 n;
                  g2 d
                }
                | false => {
                  let outside = std.rand.draw n;
                  let g = k outside;
                  let g1 = g state;
                  let g2 = g1 last;
                  g2 divisor
                }
          } }
        }
      };
      let s1 = stepped seed;
      let s2 = s1 w;
      s2 1
    }
